@@ -60,3 +60,11 @@ Year means the official conference edition label (e.g. CVPR 2020), regardless of
 ## Lossless source storage
 
 See [the source storage protocol](scripts/CATALOGUE_SOURCE_STORAGE.md). Source shards preserve every original byte and field. The three legacy working files are ignored generated copies; existing editing and QA scripts keep their APIs. After a deliberate data update, validate and capture it before building or saving source. Hydration never overwrites uncaptured edits. This storage change does not increase the existing 32 MiB raw or 8 MiB gzip application limits.
+
+## Versioned complete-data interface
+
+The hosted catalogue loads all records from `/data/papers-v1/manifest.json` and content-addressed bounded pages. It exposes no partial catalogue or partial Insights. `/data/papers-v1/download.html` provides a complete byte-exact JSON download after length/hash verification, plus accessible ordered page links without JavaScript. The original `/data/papers.json` keeps its exact full-array, GET/HEAD/range/ETag behavior while the complete response fits its existing 32 MiB raw and 8 MiB gzip bounds.
+
+If either bound is exceeded, the hosted Worker returns HTTP 409 with a `catalogue_requires_paging` problem and links to the versioned complete-data alternatives. It never substitutes a subset, manifest, redirect or stale array. HEAD has the same status/links and no body; POST remains 405. Clients should use the versioned manifest and verify the complete ordered page set, or use the verified complete download.
+
+Above the legacy bounds, generic static hosting/GitHub Pages is not supported without an equivalent reviewed non-200 error route. An explicitly static hosting configuration fails the build. Deploy only the official Worker artifact, not the preparatory static directory. No existing response or package limit is raised.
